#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:2 7479995e5f244ce297ab4ea516abb4b8
msgid "A tape as a filesystem: LTFS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:4 00214b2d4c1946968336b88390847afb
msgid ""
"LTFS puts a filesystem on a cartridge, so you can copy files on and off "
"it with ``cp`` and ``ls`` instead of a backup program. It is a separate "
"project from MHVTL, used mostly for archives — a tape you will read again"
" in ten years, by someone who no longer has the software that wrote it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:9 97cff61e7b174fb3886ac8ffe9b87760
msgid ""
"The console does not make every tape an LTFS volume. It is an extra, and "
"it has to be asked for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:12 9f103602fb994ed6b3b140216a044be4
msgid ""
"Everything below was run against library 80, a StorageTek SL500 created "
"for the purpose and deleted at the end. The same sequence is the "
"recording in ``recordings/ltfs-on-a-cartridge``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:21 0f07dd00e7af4392b25b6ea949a9e235
msgid "Two different things are called \"mount\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:23 764013b5b3a04d969e66e396f2363d8c
msgid "This is the thing to keep straight before anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:30 e3fa590742b74e098f70751cf315e6e6
msgid "**Mount a tape**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:31 dd869dc8dff44fd7b186cb78d733fef2
msgid "**Mount LTFS**"
msgstr ""

