msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:38 1dff0708f8b74f1cbe337734b467dab2
msgid "Needs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:39 b4185e2eadf34581809b7ea50ab39da6
msgid "a free drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:40 71aad95f31e84153a88d8f940e202679
msgid "a cartridge in a drive, a drive LTFS will open, and an LTFS volume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:42 ba7baf25a12a4a0fb8d44f958ef433b5
msgid "You always do the first before the second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:45 c5d95bcb378e41babadb7708f70090d8
msgid "1. Can this library do LTFS at all?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:47 488779f7040844938a001da3f8f0c075
msgid ""
"Ask before anything else. Most libraries cannot, and the answer costs "
"nothing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:71 30e5febcb10e4e95ac50622a0ee7b433
msgid ""
"Read the last line of the table: **not read**, not \"none\". No cartridge"
" in this library was looked at, because no drive here could have opened "
"one. A cartridge nobody read may still be an LTFS volume written "
"somewhere else, and the console will not say otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:76 ab964ea403354279ac68f7e7e14bba47
msgid ""
"LTFS refuses these drives for their **vendor id**, not their model. It "
"knows IBM and HP and does not know ``STK``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:80 b85fd205cc4b4a0082f32cc527c6d79d
msgid "2. Give it a drive LTFS will open"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:82 bbf8d58b30b548e28c198a6f12bbb409
msgid ""
"The drives are emulated, so the vendor id a drive reports is yours to "
"choose. The library's own profile decides which models it will take; LTFS"
" decides which vendor ids it will open. Picking one that satisfies both "
"is all this does:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:98 5784f4d7203d4a35910f47a91be02f4e
msgid ""
"Nothing existing is changed. **A drive is only ever added** — no drive is"
" overwritten, no personality is altered, and the drives that were there "
"keep reporting exactly what they reported before. Removing a drive is a "
"separate job on the drives pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:113 aafc9ba7e1a24ac389fe596c3114fc5c
msgid ""
"The **NODE** column is the one to check. A drive with no device node is "
"not usable, whatever the other columns say."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:116 90438997b278448ea7bf39b412baee9d
msgid ""
"Some drives also need a minimum firmware: IBM LTO-5 wants B170, LTO-8 "
"wants HB81. ``--drive-revision`` sets it, and the refusal tells you when "
"you need it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:120 7d270053008243b99fb0ca1574ebf087
msgid "3. A cartridge it can write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:122 1043ac5dd83a49d3b7aaaee2017ed269
msgid ""
"Being partitionable is not enough. ``mkltfs`` **writes**, so the "
"cartridge has to be a density the drive can write, not merely load — an "
"LTO-7 drive loads LTO-5 read-only, so an LTO-5 cartridge in it can never "
"become a volume:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:144 4a3cbe08fc7d43dda404e77154d4d4ab
msgid ""
"The three T10000 cartridges came with the library and the new drive "
"cannot write any of them. ``K80004L7`` is the one that can become a "
"volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:148 3273e86a682340258e0f80149005dcaf
msgid "4. Put it in the drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:150 fe2e712e8d274327a1376e030e960b7d
msgid "The robot, not the filesystem — the first sense of \"mount\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:164 d33684c315824dea992332b23b9dd4bf
msgid ""
"``op layout`` draws the whole library — drives, slots, the import/export "
"port and a legend — coloured by tape generation. On the web it is "
"**Operator → Mount and Unmount**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:169 c5117bd2a8904caebf8eec2c1ca3b979
msgid "5. Format it — which the console will not do for you"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:173 f53849564ae44efa8b75707173e9f5b1
msgid ""
"``mkltfs`` partitions and erases the cartridge. Everything on it is gone,"
" and there is no undo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:176 d1d50b0c7e1f407d924ddffebc6e21ea
msgid ""
"The console refuses, twice over — a setting it checks, and a ``sudoers`` "
"rule the service account was never granted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:188 0ce5d3a5869841ac924d42ca8fc3c7df
msgid ""
"That is deliberate, and it is not an obstacle to work around. Formatting "
"a cartridge stays an act a person takes at a terminal, with root, having "
"decided to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:198 9d717d2b79eb43339078f28c4fdaa5a9
msgid "The device is the **NODE** from ``ltfs drives``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:201 c4588c8f34e643ec8a82defd436c171a
msgid "6. Mount it, write to it, read it back"
msgstr ""

