msgid "Now the second sense of \"mount\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:210 5b0f4d4c5a95410a9bc0bc9367a64ae7
msgid "It is a directory. Write to it with anything:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:220 2b85d05585d44a33840856d366082a7b
msgid ""
"And the proof that it is on the tape rather than in a cache — unmount, "
"mount again, and check:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:236 b0d211193d7d43ac972cc6f33d9b6026
msgid "7. Taking it out again, in the right order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:238 c4b35be471b54c9cb8a2b8abf0046aa1
msgid ""
"The filesystem first, then the robot. If you try it the other way the "
"console stops you:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../using/ltfs.rst:252 972892929c9b4c40baa0988be665c362
msgid ""
"This is a refusal and not a warning. Taking the cartridge out leaves "
"``ltfs`` holding a device with no medium; whatever was reading the mount "
"gets errors instead of an ending. On the mount page such a drive is "
"marked and cannot be clicked, and ``op layout`` marks it **MOUNTED**."
msgstr ""

